Z||000000||DreXteR||08-27-2001||11:11 AM||||Well is noactually a madness but the solution maybe will be expensive. <P>The situation: I want to replace the brake lines for the earls ss brake lines form Fierostore. I try to take the rubber old ones from the car but havent succed! They are stuck almost welded. Maybe the previous owner use some locktite or something. Trying to take them off, the area where the tool engage to take it off get damage. As seen here(this pic is in good order, its just to show the area):<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/damage.bmp"> <P>Solutions: The only 2 things that came into my head are: 1.Cut the tip with a round tube cutter and place a new fitting-also to make the flare. 2.Buy the ss lines that are in sell on ebay- those are for $175  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>What should I do??????<P>Thanx for the words of wisdom.<P>DreX||||reg||1
